{
  "$comment": [
    "The chat SSE contract, as frames on the wire and what a client must make of them.",
    "",
    "Read by every client's parser test. Neither client owns this file; a change here",
    "breaks both at once, in CI, which is the point — the desktop and the phone share",
    "no code, and four divergences had already accumulated silently between them.",
    "",
    "The backend's side is api/chat.py: _sse() for named events, _yield_chunk() for text,",
    "_SSE_DONE for the terminator, _SSE_KEEPALIVE while a command is buffered.",
    "",
    "The rule that makes 'unknown event' detectable: text chunks carry NO 'event:' line.",
    "Every named event has one. So an unrecognised name is an unrecognised event, never",
    "text — which is what both clients used to get wrong.",
    "Frames marked \"synthetic\" are not emitted by the backend: `skill` never was — both clients carry it in a skip-list that predates the contract — and the unknown-event case is invented on purpose. They pin client behaviour, so the backend's coverage test ignores them."
  ],
  "frames": [
    {
      "name": "plain text chunk has no event line",
      "raw": "data: Привет",
      "expect": {
        "type": "text",
        "chunk": "Привет"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "multi-line text is rejoined with newlines",
      "raw": "data: first\ndata: second",
      "expect": {
        "type": "text",
        "chunk": "first\nsecond"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "an empty line inside a chunk survives",
      "raw": "data: a\ndata: \ndata: b",
      "expect": {
        "type": "text",
        "chunk": "a\n\nb"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "text that looks like JSON stays text",
      "raw": "data: {\"not\": \"an event\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "text",
        "chunk": "{\"not\": \"an event\"}"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "terminator",
      "raw": "data: [DONE]",
      "expect": {
        "type": "done"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "pair_id — always first, and the only handle for deleting a broken pair",
      "raw": "event: pair_id\ndata: {\"pair_id\": \"3f2b\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "pair_id",
        "pairId": "3f2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "rewrite replaces the shown text, never appends",
      "raw": "event: rewrite\ndata: {\"text\": \"final answer\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "rewrite",
        "text": "final answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "memory carries the recalled facts",
      "raw": "event: memory\ndata: {\"chroma_facts\": [{\"id\": \"1\", \"text\": \"t\", \"category\": \"c\", \"impressive\": 3, \"time_label\": \"вчера\"}]}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "memory",
        "chromaFacts": [
          {
            "id": "1",
            "text": "t",
            "category": "c",
            "impressive": 3,
            "time_label": "вчера"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "error must surface as an error, not as reply text",
      "raw": "event: error\ndata: {\"message\": \"upstream refused\", \"pair_id\": \"3f2b\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "error",
        "message": "upstream refused"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "error with no message still parses as an error",
      "raw": "event: error\ndata: {\"pair_id\": \"3f2b\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "error",
        "message": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "image_start",
      "raw": "event: image_start\ndata: {\"prompt\": \"a cat\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "image_start",
        "prompt": "a cat"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "image_ready",
      "raw": "event: image_ready\ndata: {\"path\": \"/api/generated_images/a.png\", \"model\": \"m\", \"prompt\": \"a cat\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "image_ready",
        "path": "/api/generated_images/a.png",
        "model": "m",
        "prompt": "a cat"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "image_cancel carries nothing",
      "raw": "event: image_cancel\ndata: {}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "image_cancel"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "known but not consumed: skill",
      "raw": "event: skill\ndata: {\"name\": \"web_search\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "skip",
        "event": "skill"
      },
      "synthetic": true
    },
    {
      "name": "known but not consumed: web_results",
      "raw": "event: web_results\ndata: {\"sources\": []}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "skip",
        "event": "web_results"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "known but not consumed: image_urls",
      "raw": "event: image_urls\ndata: {\"urls\": [\"/api/user_uploads/a.png\"]}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "skip",
        "event": "image_urls"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "known but not consumed: search_start",
      "raw": "event: search_start\ndata: {\"query\": \"q\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "skip",
        "event": "search_start"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "known but not consumed: search_results",
      "raw": "event: search_results\ndata: {\"pairs\": []}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "skip",
        "event": "search_results"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "known but not consumed: web_start",
      "raw": "event: web_start\ndata: {\"query\": \"q\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "skip",
        "event": "web_start"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "known but not consumed: web_done",
      "raw": "event: web_done\ndata: {\"query\": \"q\"}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "skip",
        "event": "web_done"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "an event the client has never heard of is skipped, NOT shown as text",
      "raw": "event: something_added_next_release\ndata: {\"x\": 1}",
      "expect": {
        "type": "skip",
        "event": "something_added_next_release"
      },
      "synthetic": true
    },
    {
      "name": "a named event with unparseable data is skipped, not shown",
      "raw": "event: memory\ndata: {not json",
      "expect": {
        "type": "skip",
        "event": "memory"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a keepalive comment is not an event at all",
      "raw": ": keepalive",
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "a frame with no data line is not an event",
      "raw": "event: rewrite",
      "expect": null
    }
  ],
  "buffering": [
    {
      "name": "two complete frames and nothing left over",
      "buffer": "data: a\n\ndata: b\n\n",
      "events": [
        "data: a",
        "data: b"
      ],
      "remainder": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "a frame cut in half stays in the remainder",
      "buffer": "data: a\n\nevent: rew",
      "events": [
        "data: a"
      ],
      "remainder": "event: rew"
    },
    {
      "name": "nothing complete yet",
      "buffer": "data: par",
      "events": [],
      "remainder": "data: par"
    },
    {
      "name": "a keepalive between two chunks does not disturb the split",
      "buffer": "data: a\n\n: keepalive\n\ndata: b\n\n",
      "events": [
        "data: a",
        ": keepalive",
        "data: b"
      ],
      "remainder": ""
    }
  ]
}
